). All three material outcomes of the task are satisfied with direct, coherent evidence. The only blemish is a small, low-risk leftover /etc/fstab backup file from the edit step.","limitations":["The setuid functional proof conflates nosuid and noexec: since noexec already blocks all execution on both mounts, the evidence shows the SUID bit is retained in file metadata but does not independently isolate nosuid's effect from noexec's effect. This does not undermine the mount-option outcome (both options are confirmed present via findmnt) but slightly weakens the standalone functional demonstration of nosuid specifically.","No cleanup of the /etc/fstab.bak.* backup file was observed in the captured command timeline; it may still exist on node1."]},"ttft_ms":12932,"type":"result","duration_ms":44393,"uuid":"5679e1e0-f4e1-4d69-8cca-2be9b7fe47c7","ttft_stream_ms":1060,"time_to_request_ms":286,"first_content_frame_ms":1060,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
